#N canvas 40 40 1200 840 range-check 0;
#X text 20 20 The raw value arrives after the clamped one \, off the trigger's left outlet \, so the comparison always has the clamped value to compare against., f 58;
#X obj 20 170 inlet;
#X obj 20 270 !=;
#X obj 240 170 r \$0-clamped;
#X obj 20 220 change;
#X obj 20 320 select 1;
#X msg 20 370 warn u_tempo bpm-out-of-range;
#X obj 20 420 s err;
#X text 20 490 The change filters the value \, not the verdict \, so a different out-of-range value still warns., f 58;
#X text 20 660 select 1's reject goes nowhere (C-8). bpm-out-of-range is 16 characters (C-12)., f 58;
#X connect 1 0 4 0;
#X connect 4 0 2 0;
#X connect 3 0 2 1;
#X connect 2 0 5 0;
#X connect 5 0 6 0;
#X connect 6 0 7 0;
#X restore 700 400 pd range-check;
#N canvas 40 40 1300 820 realtime-out 0;
#X text 20 20 The clock and the transport go to two ports: 1 \, the Launchpad \, and 3 \, the SP-404 \, whose BPM SYNC learns tempo only from pulse intervals. A third port takes the panic STOP alone \, to the right., f 58;
#X obj 20 200 r \$0-rt;
#X obj 20 250 t f f;
#X obj 20 320 midiout;
#X obj 300 320 midiout;
#X obj 700 150 loadbang;
#X obj 700 195 t b b b;
#X msg 700 250 1;
#X msg 860 250 3;
#X text 20 420 The port goes into the cold inlet at load: Pd 0.49 does not warn about an extra creation argument \, so one could not be confirmed (item 63)., f 58;
#X text 20 570 A nonexistent port is dropped in silence \, so on the Mac port 3 costs nothing., f 58;
#X text 20 690 Two ports is a fan-out \, so a trigger (C-3). The port-4 box has its own receive and is not part of it., f 58;
#X obj 580 200 r \$0-rt4;
#X obj 580 320 midiout;
#X msg 1020 250 4;
#X text 580 420 ⛔ PORT 4 GETS THE PANIC STOP AND NOT THE CLOCK \, and the separate receive is what makes that true. \$0-rt4 is written in exactly one place -- the panic branch on the parent canvas -- so no clock byte can reach it however this file is edited later. Item 279 measured ports 2 and 4 getting NOTHING at all \, which is a bug for the Volca: it is a synthesizer with a sequencer \, and one still running through a panic is the case panic exists for. ⚠️ WIDENING THE CLOCK TO ALL FOUR IS A SEPARATE QUESTION and is parked in plan-v04 -- the Launchpad ignores incoming clock in Programmer Mode \, so ONE of the two ports fed above is already pointless \, and which devices Cut It intends to DRIVE has to be decided before adding more. The Volca honors Start/Stop only when its own MIDI Clock src is set to Auto -- that is Korg's documentation and has not been measured here \, so it is a bench step rather than an assumption. See ref/device/volca.md., f 44;
